{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>For I cannot do.</b> This is the punishment of the angels — for having said ״כִּי מַשְׁחִיתִים אֲנַחְנוּ״, attributing the matter to themselves. Therefore they did not move from there until they were forced to say that the matter is not in their authority." "<b>For I cannot.</b> Singular; from here you learn that one destroys and one saves — for two angels are not sent for one task." "<b>Therefore the name of the city was called Zoar.</b> After the name וְהִיא מִצְעָר."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:31.583024167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}